  "limits": [
    "Synthetic native GDI wrappers inject one FillRect failure with partial red painting, one DeleteDC failure and one bitmap deletion failure per launch. This is API-return failure qualification, not actual GDI resource exhaustion.",
    "A persistent real deletion failure deliberately retains the task, canvas state and existing task timer and retries on later100ms ticks. It does not spin or abandon ownership; indefinite/permanent-failure UI behavior is not otherwise qualified.",
    "Four native runs use matched current TR51616/TR53216 on private TandyHX 8088/640KB Windows3.0 real-mode fixtures. Other native modes, physical mouse actions, long-duration exhaustion and physical hardware remain unqualified.",
    "The library helper C/H and its existing ABI/color/damage/copy tests are unchanged and reused. The sample message-loop changed, so normal and injected actual-WinMain tests were repeated; earlier sample binaries are not presented as the fixed runtime.",
    "No push, PR, release, approval, merge or BOR/Mesen interaction."
  ],
  "evidence": "Full raw logs/configs/captures, failed controls, build inputs and patch verification retained in private CUBEVAL validation archive. No foreign tools or OS media bundled."
